          %p
          #ExampleOfHypergeometricKZEquations.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Hypergeometric Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov equations)
              %br/
              Let
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_X \colon X \to B
                  be the forgetful map of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
                  from Ex.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ForgetfulMapBetweenConfigurationSpaces"}
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Conf
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi Conf
                          %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Conf_{n + N}(\mathbb{R}^2)
                        \\xrightarrow{\;\;}
                        Conf_{N}(\mathbb{R}^2)
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \,=\, K(\mathbb{C},n)
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
                  classifying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cohomology"} complex cohomology
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi k
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \,\coloneqq\, \mathbb{Z}/k \,\subset\, U(1)
                  be a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/roots+of+unity"} roots of unity
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℂ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                  and hence on
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℂ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{C},n)
            %p
              Then Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiberwiseTwistedNonAbelianCohomologySetsFormLocalSystem"}
              constructs the Gauss-Manin connection claimed in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#EtingofFrenkelKirillov98"} Etingof, Frenkel &amp; Kirillov 1998, §7.5
